      <div class="smc-testi__more-wrap">
        <a
          href="https://www.google.com/maps/place/Joe%27s+Vintage+Guitars+-+We+Buy+Guitars!/@33.420432,-111.8365821,17z/data=!4m7!3m6!1s0x872ba7d2937937d9:0x69728d089b8a764!8m2!3d33.420432!4d-111.8343934!9m1!1b1"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="smc-btn smc-btn--rust"
        >
          View More
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6. Inherited collection appraisal and purchase information -->
  <section id="inherited-guitar-collection" class="smc-inherited smc-anchor">
    <div class="smc-inner">
      <div class="smc-inherited__title">
        <h2 class="smc-inherited__main">Inherited A Guitar Collection And Need To Get It Appraised <span>& Sell It?</span></h2>
        <h3 class="smc-inherited__sub">We Buy Vintage Acoustic & Electric Guitar Collections In <span>Any State</span></h3>
      </div>
      <div class="smc-inherited__grid">
        <div class="smc-inherited__text">
          <p>If you’ve just become the owner of a guitar collection and have no idea what it’s worth or where to start, I can help. I’ll travel to you anywhere in the United States for <a href="/free-appraisal/" class="smc-link">in-person guitar appraisals</a>, or we can set up an online meeting instead.</p>
          <p>I want you to understand what the guitar is actually worth. I won’t cut corners or make anything up. I love vintage guitars, and that’s what drives everything I do. If you’d like a <a href="/free-appraisal/" class="smc-link">free appraisal</a> for your vintage guitar, email me at <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`} class="smc-link">{contact.email}</a> or text me at <a href={`sms:${contact.tel}`} class="smc-link">{contact.phone}</a>.</p>
          <div class="smc-inherited__checklist">
            <h3>Before An Estate Collection Appraisal</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Keep original cases, receipts, old appraisals, parts, straps, and paperwork with the instruments.</li>
              <li>Leave cleaning and repairs until the guitars have been examined. The wrong product or replacement part can affect a vintage instrument.</li>
              <li>Take wide photos of the rooms, racks, or cases. You don’t need to identify or unpack every instrument first.</li>
              <li>Set aside any instruments your family wants to keep before asking for a final purchase offer.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="smc-inherited__cta">
            <p><strong>Get A Free Appraisal For Your Vintage Guitar!</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="smc-inherited__photo">
          <LicensedImage
            src={imgMeta("blog5.jpg")}
            alt="Appraise And Sell Your Inherited Guitar Collection At Joe’s Vintage Guitars"
            width={340}
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6b. Honest comparison of the main collection-selling routes -->
  <section id="collection-selling-options" class="smc-options smc-anchor">
    <div class="smc-inner">
      <div class="smc-options__header">
        <p class="smc-options__eyebrow">Choose The Route That Fits Your Situation</p>
        <h2>Ways To Sell A Guitar Collection</h2>
        <p>There is no single route for every seller. The right choice depends on how much time you have, how quickly the collection needs to move, and whether your priority is convenience or the highest possible total from individual sales.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="smc-options__grid">
